2 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 8.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.2 to 14.6. December accounts for 13% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. Contract [1], for 14,990 euros, was awarded in December 2025. Contract [3], for 14,900 euros, was awarded in November 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar amounts under the limit can result from market prices or budget constraints. The data reflects statistical trends, not individual misconduct.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for consistent pricing and compare them to other contracts for the same service. Review the November contract to see if it follows the same pattern. Ensure no single supplier is used repeatedly for the same need.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["QXC%2B23qd9iCLAncw3qdZkA%3D%3D","MNH2m3LZl10S7pcxhTeWOg%3D%3D","XZHz0CbEGpM%2B1TMyIiZmzw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}